+`docs/adr/ADR-001-nestjs.md`:
+```markdown
+# ADR-001: Why NestJS
+
+## Status
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+We need a Node.js framework for building a production-grade notification platform. The framework must support TypeScript, dependency injection, modular architecture, and enterprise patterns.
+
+## Decision
+Use NestJS as the application framework.
+
+## Rationale
+- **Modular architecture**: NestJS modules map directly to our service boundaries
+- **Dependency injection**: Built-in DI container promotes testability and SOLID principles
+- **Monorepo support**: Native monorepo mode with apps and libraries
+- **Decorator-based**: Clean controller, service, and module definitions
+- **Ecosystem**: Terminus, OpenTelemetry, Swagger integrations are first-class
+- **Testing**: NestJS testing utilities simplify unit and integration tests
+- **TypeScript-first**: Full TypeScript support with strict mode from day one
+
+## Consequences
+- Services are coupled to NestJS-specific APIs
+- Learning curve for developers unfamiliar with Angular-style DI
+- Build toolchain (SWC/Webpack) adds complexity
+```
+
